commit 66f131b00482af027bc83b9786d85d9050a6dec4
Author: conquerthecrowns <bryce@choquercreative.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 24 15:34:18 2026 -0700

    feat(ai): human-prose guard, voice consistency rule, 75k preference limit
    
    Closes two writer flags (2026-08-23, 3GA Marine):
    - RULES_VOICE_CONSISTENCY: in mandated-opener paragraphs voice follows
      sentence function (neutral for mechanisms, we/our for team actions) with
      explicit precedence over the company-as-subject rule; QA checks it with a
      firstPersonRequested flag derived from the writer's preferences
    - MAX_INSTRUCTIONS_CHARS 60k -> 75k, shared by server validation, counters,
      style analysis, and the chat agent (was silently sliced at 20k)
    
    Human prose (no-em-dashes + plain-language rules), always on:
    - shared/humanProse.ts: RULES_HUMAN_PROSE block and findDashConnectors()
      deterministic scanner (em dash, --, spaced hyphen, spaced en dash; ignores
      compounds, ranges, closed en dashes, equation minus, line structure)
    - dash_connector findings in section review and the QA pre-computed checks;
      compression pass told not to reintroduce dashes; chat replies covered
    - every system prompt recast to be dash-clean itself (test enforces it)
    - locked-rules catalogue and admin house-rules page list both new rules
    
    Also carries the in-progress PSOS-42..50 house-style governance work
    (houseStyle, styleOverrides, writerStyle, admin/house-rules) that these
    changes build on.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

